{"repositoryId":541560084,"availability":"available","full":"eclipse-epsilon/epsilon","name":"epsilon","description":"Epsilon is a family of Java-based scripting languages for automating common model-based software engineering tasks, such as code generation, model-to-model transformation and model validation, that work out of the box with EMF (including Xtext and Sirius), UML (including Cameo/MagicDraw), Simulink, XML and other types of models.","category":"Design","language":"Java","stars":106,"forks":16,"created":"2022-09-26T11:52:37Z","updated":"2026-10-16T16:21:34Z","license":"EPL-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://eclipse.org/epsilon","topics":["domain-specific-languages","model-based-software-engineering","model-driven-engineering"],"demo":"https://eclipse.dev/epsilon/playground/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T16:00:49.416Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T16:00:49.416Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T16:00:49.416Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-17T16:00:49.416Z","stars":106,"forks":16}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Epsilon is a family of scripting languages and tools for automating common model-based software engineering tasks such as code generation, model-to-model transformation, model validation and model visualisation, that work out of the box with EMF (including Xtext and Sirius), UML (including Cameo/MagicDraw), Simulink, XML and other types of models.","Epsilon can be used as a standard Java library, and also provides Apache Ant tasks that can be embedded in Maven/Gradle builds. Editing support for Epsilon programs is available in Eclipse, VS Code and Sublime."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/eclipse-epsilon/epsilon/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"fded3a3ae981159fab800c39a55e8f5476ca97e4183a306d036a5539fda581ca","extractedAt":"2026-10-17T16:00:49.580Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T16:00:49.580Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Epsilon is